## ***********************************************************************
## **
## **  MENU.INC.BANKED.BL -- the menu store's banked groups, and the sizes
## **  that describe them. #INCLUDE it straight before MENU.INC.BL.
## **
## **  The bar's 16 rows, then the popup's 32, then, in the text group only,
## **  the dropdown pool's 64. A row is one SPC line, so a .MAX define and
## **  its SPC lines are written here together and cannot drift apart.
## **
## **  #INCLUDE it and the program gets a .OVL beside its .PRG: the groups
## **  are banked, and banked data travels in a file of its own in every
## **  build. Ship both files together.
## **
## ***********************************************************************
## A group must be declared before GP.BSTR names it, so this comes first.
#IFNDEF MENU.TEXTBANK
#DEFINE MENU.TEXTBANK 62
#ENDIF

## How many rows each slot holds. MENU.POOLBASE is where the pool starts in the
## text group, which is every bar row and every popup row before it, so it is
## MENU.BAR.MAX + MENU.POPUP.MAX and nothing else. The text group is that many
## rows plus the pool; the hint group is that many rows, because only the bar
## and the popup keep hints.
#DEFINE MENU.BAR.MAX 16
#DEFINE MENU.POPUP.MAX 32
#DEFINE MENU.POOL.MAX 64
#DEFINE MENU.POOLBASE 48

GOTO MENU.BANKED.END

